## Repair complete

**Root cause of gate failure (attempt 1):** not a mathematics/proof error. The harness gate runs `lake env lean <file>` with the **worktree root** as cwd, but this worktree's Lake package lives in `release/`. With no root `lean-toolchain`/`lakefile.toml`, elan aborted every file with `error: no default toolchain configured`, so all 75 `.lean` files failed. (The deleted `gate.json` was consumed by the dispatcher when it queued the repair; I re-derived the failure by running the gate command myself.)

**Fix (scaffold only — no `.lean` file touched):**
| root file | content |
|---|---|
| `lakefile.toml` | root package `VerifierD7AdversarialAuditRoot`, `packagesDir = ".lake/packages"`, `require mathlib` |
| `lean-toolchain` | copy of `release/lean-toolchain` (`leanprover/lean4:v4.34.0-rc2`) |
| `lake-manifest.json` | copy of `release/lake-manifest.json` (mathlib `7974e751…`) |
| `.lake` | symlink to `release/.lake` (prebuilt pinned mathlib + release oleans) |

This re-exposes the prebuilt package tree so the gate's exact command resolves the pinned toolchain/mathlib offline — the same scaffold the two passing D7 worktrees use.

